WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:02.980
Well, I have some very
urgent news to report.

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:03.813
You guys ready?

00:00:03.813 --> 00:00:04.646
Yeah.

00:00:04.646 --> 00:00:06.200
You got your urgent news hats on

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:07.390
because this is big stuff?

00:00:07.390 --> 00:00:08.809
This must be so important.

00:00:08.809 --> 00:00:09.642
It must be important.

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:10.475
Sounds serious.

00:00:10.475 --> 00:00:11.308
Yeah.

00:00:11.308 --> 00:00:14.180
Last week, I was in the Larchmont area

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:19.180
of Los Angeles with our producing deity.

00:00:19.270 --> 00:00:20.700
The God, he's the man behind the scenes

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:22.550
who pulls the strings, Mr. Adam Sachs.

00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:25.650
We were at this meeting in a building

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:29.450
and it was a, listen, this
is going somewhere important.

00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:30.283
I'm sorry.

00:00:30.283 --> 00:00:32.420
We were in this meeting,
building. (laughs)

00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:34.800
Meeting in a in a building in Larchmont.

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:37.340
And of course everyone's
socially distancing.

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:38.410
There's not that many people there.

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:39.530
We've got our masks on.

00:00:39.530 --> 00:00:40.940
It's all very safe.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:43.070
And then we realized there's a balcony.

00:00:43.070 --> 00:00:44.810
So we go out on the balcony

00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:46.470
just to be able to breathe some air.

00:00:46.470 --> 00:00:48.940
And it's Adam Sachs and I on the balcony

00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:52.290
and we're on the third floor,
not that high up on a balcony.

00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:56.340
And I looked down and
there's a young couple.

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:57.730
I want to say a man and a woman.

00:00:57.730 --> 00:01:02.023
I'm going to say in their late
twenties, maybe 25, 28, 29.

00:01:02.860 --> 00:01:04.710
And they've been standing there

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:06.440
and they're just looking up

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:07.690
and I walk out on the balcony

00:01:07.690 --> 00:01:09.927
and just as they see me, the guys says,

00:01:09.927 --> 00:01:13.920
"Kedakai, as God made her!"

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:15.370
Oh this makes me so happy.

00:01:15.370 --> 00:01:18.170
And I was on top of this
balcony, like Mussolini.

00:01:18.170 --> 00:01:20.220
And I was like, "Yes!"

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:21.390
And they were like, "Yay."

00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:22.980
And then I went, "Kedakai!"

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:25.030
And they said, "Kedakai!"

00:01:25.030 --> 00:01:27.070
And I'm like, I don't know,

00:01:27.070 --> 00:01:32.070
it's nothing expresses
the power of a podcast

00:01:32.670 --> 00:01:34.440
more than that insane moment.

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:35.890
I mean, we're in,

00:01:35.890 --> 00:01:37.830
this country has so many problems,

00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:39.597
so many things to deal with (laughs)

00:01:39.597 --> 00:01:41.560
And you can use this for good.

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:43.030
And instead you use it

00:01:43.030 --> 00:01:44.670
so people yell this thing at you.

00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:47.670
I could be distributing
valuable information

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:49.160
on how you can go to certain websites

00:01:49.160 --> 00:01:51.940
to get the vaccine where you can go,

00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:54.510
how many times you should wash your hands.

00:01:54.510 --> 00:01:56.830
There's all kinds of
good I could be doing,

00:01:56.830 --> 00:02:01.650
instead I've spread this
foolishness across where

00:02:01.650 --> 00:02:03.700
once the Dean of the actors studio,

00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:06.690
Mr. James Lipton, I was
at a dinner with him

00:02:06.690 --> 00:02:10.560
and he pointed up to a painting
of his wife in the nude

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:13.088
And wrote "Kedakai, as God made her!"

00:02:13.088 --> 00:02:13.921
(laughs)

00:02:13.921 --> 00:02:16.100
And I've said that and
I'm obsessed with it.

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:17.650
And then I sort of challenged people

00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:21.020
and I've had people since come up to me

00:02:21.020 --> 00:02:24.743
and yell it at me, once at the
Largo Theater through a gate.

00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:28.027
And they yell it as if they've come up

00:02:28.027 --> 00:02:31.020
with the secret word
that will save the earth.

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:32.440
That's how they say it.

00:02:32.440 --> 00:02:34.600
And this, these people were, I think

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:35.950
had seen me go into the building.

00:02:35.950 --> 00:02:37.570
And I think they waited.

00:02:37.570 --> 00:02:38.403
Oh, that's good.

00:02:38.403 --> 00:02:40.890
I think they waited, and they were like

00:02:40.890 --> 00:02:42.750
he might come out at some point

00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:45.060
and we've been told we have to do this.

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:46.200
That's dedication.

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:47.033
I applaud them.

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:48.720
I don't know who you, people are.

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:52.680
You were in the Larchmont
area, but God bless you.

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:55.091
You filled my head with delusions

00:02:55.091 --> 00:02:55.924
(laughs)

00:02:55.924 --> 00:02:58.083
and you're keeping me
going for another year.

